            <ArticleTitle>Intracardiac and aortic thrombi in capuchin monkeys (Cebus apella).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>259-66</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Massive intracardiac or aortic mural thrombi, probably of septic origin, occurred in six capuchin monkeys (Cebus apella) and accounted for 26% of all adult deaths in a breeding group over a 4-yr period. Previous experimental inoculations with herpes simplex type 2 virus may have contributed to the development of these fatal lesions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
